<title>USA: Motorola wins $25 mln contract in China.</title>
<headline>Motorola wins $25 mln contract in China.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said its cellular infrastructure group has won a contract worth more than $25 million to expand and upgrade an analog Total Access Communications System (TACS) cellular network in Shandong Province, China.</p>
<p>Last March, Shandong Posts and Telecommunications awarded Motorola a $50 million contract to expand the same TACS network.</p>
<p>As a result of the upgrade, subscriber capacity will increase to 520,000 from 430,000. The expansion should be completed in early 1998, Motorola said in a news release.</p>
<p>		    ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
